last week i made a video on seven books  that completely changed my life  and then i realized that not many people  like to read so that is why i'm here to  share with you  seven tips to help you start a reading  habit even if you hate to read  these tips are inspired by the book  atomic habits by james clear  which is actually what helped me pick up  reading and  change several other habits in my life  number one  remove barriers or excuses that you  might use  for example if you fall asleep while  reading books then don't read on a bed  if you're tempted to check your cell  phone then put it away or turn it off  if your family is always watching tv  then don't read in the same room that  they're in  chances are your attention might stray  the main thing here is to think of  excuses and barriers that you might  normally use  and find a way to remove those number  two set  cues to remind you to read have you ever  tried to start a habit  and you ended up quitting on it only  because you kept forgetting to do it  for this set cues place the book where  you can't miss it  for example i had gotten out of habit of  reading my bible every night for me  that's important so what i ended up  doing was placing my bible  directly on the bed so that that way  every time  i had to undo the bed to get in i had to  physically hold the book in my hand  which was a cue to me to read it if you  plan to read on your favorite chair for  example then place it directly  on your chair or place it somewhere  nearby or if you plan to read at a  specific time  then set an alarm your cue can actually  be a habit that you already have which  is even more powerful  for example if you normally like to  drink your a cup of coffee every morning  then place your book beside your coffee  machine and  you can read while you drink your  favorite cup of coffee  number three make it pleasurable our  brains naturally want to do things that  bring us pleasure  because it brings that dopamine spike  that tells us it's rewarding  but if you hate reading you can actually  use this as leverage by using  things that you already enjoy and find  pleasurable to associate with reading  for example use your favorite comfy  chair that you like  or pour yourself a cup of coffee or tea  if that's something that you enjoy  or use warm lighting for me i love fuzzy  blankets i have one in like every room  and it helps me just kind of set the  vibe so to say and try to have a  designated place where you can read and  focus  you know maybe not right next to the  refrigerator number four  take it slow don't start off with huge  goals like reading one book per week  because it's only going to weigh you  down  the key here is to make small easy to  achieve goals that  you will repeat every day repetition is  what makes a habit  not the amount of time that you do it  for so maybe it's only reading a chapter  per day or reading 15 minutes per day  the key here is to make the goal small  so that's much more likely that this  repeated action  will become a habit number five  eliminate  idle time this is that time that you're  not really doing anything too productive  like when you're waiting for an oil  change  or during a commute if you're like me  and you drive a lot  try listening to audiobooks during your  commute okay sure you don't exactly flip  pages but you still absorb the  information  or if you're going to wait for an oil  change or wait at the doctor's office  then  just take the book with you number six  is accountability you can do this by  yourself or with other people  but the key is to make specific goals  set a specific time and location and  follow through  actually schedule it in your calendar  when you schedule something like you do  an appointment it's much more likely  that you're actually going to do it  you can also try tracking your progress  through habit tracking apps or by  journaling about what you've read  if you prefer a team approach then join  a book club  or start reading with someone that will  keep you accountable and actually  motivate you to keep going as well  and number seven choose wisely choose a  book that you will  actually enjoy i am a total science nerd  i could actually read this bad boy for  fun  but if reading about enzymes and  photosynthesis is something that would  put you to sleep  then find a book that you find  interesting through an activity or a  topic that you actually enjoy  maybe read a smaller book if pictures is  your thing find a book with pictures  you can also ask friends for  recommendations or even just read  reviews  and if you're getting bored by a book  then switch it out and start a new one  in this case you don't have to finish  what you started because the key is  to keep the habit instead of stopping  all together because this one book  is torture and if you're trying to pick  up healthy habits or cut out unhealthy  habits from your life  i highly recommend the book atomic  habits by james clear  it gives you a systematic approach to  analyzing your habits to see where you  can make small changes  to get amazing results i will leave the  link in the description  that is it for today guys if you found  any of these tips helpful please give it  a thumbs up  and subscribe so that you won't miss out  on my weekly videos i thank you so much  for watching and i can't wait to see you  in the next one
 

